Cell["\<\
Thanks . The compiler works now . However, there is a problem with the C++ \
code . Trying result = aa2fCheckExtendability[testWords, 6, 50000], one finds \
that the result cannot be right : Testing on : {aaabaaacccbccaabbbaccbcc}

Preparing data for GPU ...

Running Backtracking Solver on GPU ...

---RESULTS-- - Extendable (Good) : 0

NonExtendable (Bad) : 1

Undecided (Timeout) : 0 Namely, \"aaabaaacccbccaabbbaccbcc\" already has 28 \
extensions when extended 6 to the left and 6 to the right . Furthermore, it \
has 1352 extensions when extended 10 to the left and 10 to the right . My \
Mathematica function aa2fInt32MakeFreeWordUsingList3let (code is not included \
here) shows this . I used it like this : myRes = \
Flatten[aa2fInt32MakeFreeWordUsingList3let[StringReverse[#] <> \
\"ABFGHJLMPQ\"] & /@ \
aa2fInt32MakeFreeWordUsingList3let[\"aaabaaacccbccaabbbaccbcc\" <> \
\"ABFGHJLMPQ\", 25]], and after 32 seconds, I see a list of extended words, \
1352 in total .\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9776340696303043`*^9, 
  3.9776340934975166`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"975d25f4-1653-b046-b410-\
bf8f53c676d5"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Functions aa2fInt32Parikh, aa2fInt32CreateList3let, \
aa2fInt32MakeFreeWordUsingList3let, aa2fInt32PickVariables3let, \
aa2fInt32TestList3let, aa2fInt32SolveList3let, where \
aa2fInt32MakeFreeWordUsingList3let is the main function.\
\>", "Subsection",
